# Read the rules first — NON-NEGOTIABLE

Before adding or changing documentation in **Detis Engine Documentation** (`detis_engine_docs`):

1. Re-read **`.cursor/rules/code-examples.mdc`** if the change includes fenced code or API names.
2. Re-read **`.cursor/rules/ascii-markdown.mdc`** for any **`.md`** edit.
3. Re-read **`.cursor/rules/manual-voice.mdc`** if the change is under **`manuals/`**, **`tutorials/`**, or **`getting_started/`**.
4. Re-read **`.cursor/rules/sequential-navigation.mdc`** when adding or reordering multi-page guides or **`## Continue reading`** footers.

Do not rely on memory from an earlier chat. If the change type matches a rule file and you have not opened it this turn, do not edit yet.

## Hard stops

- Em dash (—) anywhere in Markdown you edit. Use **:** or ** - ** instead.
- Unicode arrows (**→**, **←**, etc.) in Markdown you edit. Use **`->`** or **`<-`** instead.
- Generic **scene** / **level** / **map** when the engine means **world** (**`.world`**, world script, **`world_load_*`**, **View -> World Settings**).
- Terminology not found in stubs, editor labels, or existing docs (invented synonyms).
- Invented API identifiers or **`...`** inside example calls.
- Paste-ready fences with undefined globals.
- Front-loading advanced flags, wrappers, or layering before the simple working path.
- Turning beginner pages into internal engine design notes.
